    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164:\n\n1. **`CountryCallingCode.java`** \u2014 added a small `code()` accessor so the calling code (e.g. `\"61\"`) can be read. This enum was already the single authority on which E.164 calling codes the app recognises, so it's the right place to expose the code/national boundary.\n\n2. **`TelephoneDisplayFormatter.java`** (new) \u2014 a focused util with one responsibility: given a stored E.164 value, it reuses `CountryCallingCode.forDigits` to identify the calling code, then renders `\"+<code> <national digits grouped in threes>\"` (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It returns `null` for null/blank input and leaves an unrecognised calling code unchanged (no known split point).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a new `telephoneDisplay` mapping via the same expression pattern as the other derived fields, computed from `owner.getTelephone()`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema so the DTO getter/setter is generated.\n\nThe targeted acceptance test (`+61 412 345 678` from input `0412 345 678`) and the full suite both pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
